<title>PORTUGAL: EIB provides loans for Portuguese projects.</title>
<headline>EIB provides loans for Portuguese projects.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Investment Bank (EIB) said on Monday it was providing five loans totalling nearly 103 billion escudos ($670 million) for Portuguese projects.</p>
<p>The EIB will provide 15 billion escudos to Portugal Telecom for the modernisation and expansion of Portugal's telecommications network and 25 billion to the Metropolitano de Lisboa for the upgrading of the Lisbon subway system.</p>
<p>It will provide 40 billion escudos for the construction on Portugal's secondary road network, and lend 20 billion to state-owned Transgas for the construction of a natural gas pipeline from the Maghreb through Spain and Portugal.</p>
<p>The remaining 2.5 billion escudos would go to Lusitaniagas SA for investment in a local gas network in the coastal area north of Lisbon.</p>
<p>The EIB said its lending to Portugal this year had concentrated on projects to strengthen basic infrastructure.</p>
<p>($1=153.66)</p>
